  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Thresholds by Tower, Sub-tower and LOB",
      "items": [
        "rule_override sets a rule for one Tower, Sub-tower or LOB, versioned over the rule_version default.",
        "Per setting the most specific wins: LOB → Sub-tower → Tower → default; null inherits.",
        "Agent rules use the agent's home queue; queue rules also run per overridden group; every call-out keeps the version and override that fired."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Queue-to-LOB mapping",
      "items": [
        "Admin uploads the .xlsx (sheet \"Queue-to-LOB mapping\": Tower, Sub-tower, LOB, Queue); only the towers in the file are replaced.",
        "Saved to queue_lob_map (today .rtm/queue-map.json) and cached in memory for the tree, the scope resolver and the feed's watch list."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Writes never block the tick",
      "items": [
        "The engine hands records to the store, which writes them in order in batches and retries on failure.",
        "At start-up the store reloads rules, overrides, the mapping, today's shift, strikes and open call-outs and incidents.",
        "Raw events are kept for the current Eastern day only; call-outs and incidents carry over midnight."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Built today",
      "items": [
        "Phase 0: rules and their versions survive a restart (PERSISTENCE_MODE=postgres).",
        "Still in memory: shift, ledger, incidents, strikes. Build order and open decisions: docs/ideal-dataflow.md."
      ]
    }
  ]
